New LinkedIn Connection? Instant Sales Pitch Activated! 

So I accepted a connection request today.
30 seconds later: “Hi Tomas, thanks for connecting! Quick question—do you need this service?”

At this point, I’m convinced LinkedIn connections come with an automatic sales script that runs in the background like this:

if (new_connection == true) {  
  send_pitch_template_v7();  
  follow_up_in_2_days_with_case_study(); }  

Look, I get it. We’re all here to grow. But if the first message after connecting is a pitch, it feels less like networking and more like someone proposing marriage on the first date… while trying to sell me a timeshare.
